course: dictionary
lesson: 2599
title: Dependency: relying on something
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A dependency is a state of relying on someone or something. The word comes from depend, which means needing something in order to get by, and the ending -cy turns it into a noun, a naming word. «The baby's dependency on its parents» means the baby needs its parents to survive and cope. The clue is on its parents: a baby cannot look after itself, so it relies on them.
explain: Dependency has several meanings, so the context decides which one fits. «Nicotine dependency» is about a person who needs a drug and finds it very hard to stop. «The Isle of Man is a Crown Dependency» is about geography: a territory ruled by another country but not fully part of it. In computing, a dependency is a piece of code that a program needs in order to work.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the sentence around the word and ask: what depends on what? If it is about plants and animals, it means relying on each other. If it mentions a Crown, a territory or a country, it is about politics. If it mentions a program or code, it is about computing.
fact: Dependency is a noun. Its verb is depend, and its plural is dependencies.
fact: «Dependency» means relying on someone or something to survive, cope or work.
fact: «Dependency» can also mean needing a drug, alcohol or a habit and finding it very hard to stop. This is also called addiction.
fact: The Crown Dependencies, such as the Isle of Man, Jersey and Guernsey, belong to the British Crown but are not part of the UK.
fact: In computing, a project lists its dependencies: the other programs or pieces of code it needs in order to work.
exercise: In «the baby's dependency on its parents», what does dependency mean? | A piece of computer code | *Relying on someone to survive and cope | A place ruled by another country | Being very clever at maths
exercise: «The Isle of Man is a Crown Dependency.» What kind of dependency is this? | *A territory ruled by another country but not fully part of it | A food chain in a pond | A program that stops working | Nicotine addiction
exercise: A project lists its dependencies. What does dependencies mean here? | Dependent children | Holidays abroad | *Other programs or code that the project needs in order to work | Rules for a board game
test: «The Isle of Man, Jersey and Guernsey are Crown Dependencies, not part of the UK.» What are Crown Dependencies? | Large islands with the biggest farms | Countries that are fully part of the UK | *Territories ruled by another country but not fully part of it | Places with no rules at all
test: Which phrase means needing a drug and finding it very hard to stop? | Food chain | Computer program | *Drug dependency | Crown Dependency
exam: In a food chain, plants and animals show what kind of dependency? | Writing computer code | Owning a territory overseas | Being ruled by another country | *Relying on each other to survive
